cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use AXIOM in research or tooling, please cite it using this metadata.
title: "AXIOM — the transactional write gate for coding agents"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Vladulescu
    given-names: Dragos Catalin
repository-code: https://github.com/dragoscv/axiom
url: https://dragoscv.github.io/axiom/
license: MIT
version: 2.2.1
date-released: "2026-09-21"
keywords:
  - mcp
  - coding-agents
  - in-toto
  - content-addressed
  - transactional-apply
abstract: >-
  AXIOM is a transactional write gate that sits between a coding agent and the
  repository it edits. An agent describes intent as a Plan, which is compiled into
  a canonical, content-addressed Manifest (RFC 8785 JCS, sha256 digests, in-toto
  attestation). Set-level check predicates evaluate the whole change against a
  policy profile and fail closed when a fact provider cannot run. Apply is a
  hash-gated two-phase commit: the caller must echo the manifest digest, pre-image
  hashes are re-verified at commit time, writes are staged and renamed atomically
  under a single-writer lock, and a journal enables scoped rollback. AXIOM ships as
  an MCP stdio server, a CLI, a PreToolUse hook, a GitHub Action and a VS Code
  extension.
